TASK-191.1 runtime harness: a space that a link route (or the
Default) targets cannot be deleted, from the sidebar, the Settings pane, and
an undo or redo; routes persist; migration v20. Temporary code, never
committed to Detour/. Steps:

    SP=<scratch>; mkdir -p $SP/out
    git apply docs/harness/task191-1-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    APP=.derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour
    # Phase 1, fresh data dir: seed spaces Routed and Plain and a route
    # "Domain is work.test" -> Routed; delete Routed through the sidebar's own
    # deleteSpaceClicked: action, then Settings > Spaces "−" (both blocked, the
    # alert answered OK by a .common-mode timer); add an app-only route
    # (com.apple.mail) and the Default to Plain, "−" on Plain (blocked, both
    # named); remove the work.test route, sidebar delete of Routed again
    # (confirmation answered Delete: deleted).
    # Step 4: add space Undoable, route undo.test -> Undoable, Edit > Undo
    # (refused: alert; the undo stays), remove the route, Undo again (deleted).
    # Step 5: Redo (Undoable back), delete it, Undo, Default -> Undoable,
    # Redo (refused: alert; the redo stays), Default back, Redo (deleted).
    # Then 40 s idle past the GPU reapers' 30 s timers.
    # DETOUR_VERIFY_APPEARANCE=light|dark pins NSApp.appearance.
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify1911 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR=$SP/out DETOUR_VERIFY_PHASE=1 $APP &
    # Phase 2, same data dir: routes and Default read back; sidebar delete of
    # Plain still blocked.
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify1911 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR=$SP/out DETOUR_VERIFY_PHASE=2 $APP &
    # Phase 3: take the DB back to v19 by hand, relaunch, v20 runs.
    sqlite3 browser.db "DROP TABLE linkRoute; DROP TABLE linkRouteDefault;
                        DELETE FROM grdb_migrations WHERE identifier='v20';"
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify1911 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR=$SP/out DETOUR_VERIFY_PHASE=3 $APP &
    # Each phase logs to $SP/out/verify-<phase>.log; a watcher runs
    # `screencapture -x -o -l <n>` for each "SHOOT <name> <windowNumber>" line
    # (the alert's own window) while the alert is up; wait for "done", kill
    # that pid only.
    git apply -R docs/harness/task191-1-harness.patch && xcodegen generate

Edit > Undo/Redo: the harness validates the real menu item and performs its
action. When Detour is in the background (no key window, so the item is
disabled), it sends the item's action to the window controller instead and
logs that it did.

Undo grouping: the harness posts no events, so AppKit never closes the
groupsByEvent group between its steps. Steps 4 and 5 turn event grouping off
and group each action by hand (`act`), as the unit tests do. Do not end an
automatic group with endUndoGrouping: NSUndoManager then refuses the next
registration with an ObjC exception ("must begin a group before registering
undo"); thrown through the harness's Swift task and caught by AppKit, it
leaves a stale executor in TLS, and the next MainActor.assumeIsolated (the
GPU reapers' 30 s timers, RecentTabSwitcher) crashes in
swift_task_isCurrentExecutor. A first version of steps 4-5 did that; the
crash was the harness, not the app: without the hand-ended groups, no run
crashed.

Results, first run (2026-10-25, screen locked): phases 1-3 as below except
steps 4-5; no window captures (screen locked).

Results, second run (2026-10-25, screen unlocked), light and dark:
- Phase 1, fresh DB: migrations end v18,v19,v20, both tables exist. Sidebar
